---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms & Conditions — QuiiCast"
	description="The terms for using QuiiCast's free, browser-based screen sharing service."
	path="/terms"
>
	<div class="text-center">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-4xl">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
		<p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-xl text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
			The short version: it's free, it's yours to use, and you're responsible for what you share.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="prose mx-auto mt-14 max-w-2xl">
		<h2>Using QuiiCast</h2>
		<p>
			QuiiCast is provided free of charge for sharing your screen with others over a direct
			browser connection. By using it, you agree to these terms.
		</p>

		<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Don't use QuiiCast to share content you don't have the right to share, or to harass, defraud, or deceive anyone.</li>
			<li>Don't attempt to abuse the signaling server — for example, automated brute-forcing of connection codes, denial-of-service attempts, or interfering with other users' sessions.</li>
			<li>QuiiCast is designed for small-scale sharing (up to 5 concurrent viewers per cast), not for broadcasting to a large audience.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>No account, no guarantee of availability</h2>
		<p>
			QuiiCast doesn't require an account and is offered as-is, free of charge, without guarantees
			of uptime, availability, or fitness for any particular purpose. Sessions expire
			automatically and aren't guaranteed to remain available for any set period.
		</p>

		<h2>Peer-to-peer content</h2>
		<p>
			Screen sharing sessions happen directly between your browser and the browser you're
			connected to. QuiiCast does not monitor, record, or take responsibility for the content
			shared during a session — that responsibility rests with the people sharing it.
		</p>

		<h2>Third-party platforms mentioned on this site</h2>
		<p>
			QuiiCast's <a href="/blog">blog</a> and <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> occasionally reference other
			products — like Zoom, Discord, or Roku — for comparison or compatibility information.
			QuiiCast is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any of those companies.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
		<p>These terms may be updated from time to time; the current version is always the one posted on this page.</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Questions about these terms can be sent through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
